<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incīlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		contr. from incīdilis, from incido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>cut in</i>: fossae,
			i. e. <i>ditches</i>, <i>trenches</i>
			for carrying off water, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 155,
			1</span></i>.— Far more freq., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incīle</span></b> ,
			is, n., <i>a ditch</i>, <i>trench</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incilia aperire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 155, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ducere incile,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					43, 13, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 221</span></i>: in incili
			omnia adhaeserunt, Cael. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 8,
				5, 3</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incīlis</span></b> ,
			is, m., transl.: inciles <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διώρυγες</span> (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διώρυχες</span>), Gloss. Philox.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
